deep.reconstruction:
Folio 43r is mainly a non-mathematical draft. Its only legible text is a draft cover letter in ink at the top, probably addressed to the secretary of the Königliche Gesellschaft der Wissenschaften zu Göttingen. It reads roughly: 'Ew. Hochwohlgeboren habe ich die Ehre, das Manuscript meiner kürzlich der Societät vorgelegten Abhandlung beifolgend druckfertig wieder zuzusenden, mit der Bitte um Ihre Genehmigung des Drucks. [Hochachtungsvoll / ehrerbietigst …] Ew. Hochwohlgeboren [ergebenster].' In English: 'I have the honour to return the manuscript of my memoir, recently presented to the Society, ready for printing, and ask your approval for its printing.'

Given the bundle 'Luftwellen', the memoir is almost certainly 'Über die Fortpflanzung ebener Luftwellen von endlicher Schwingungsweite'. It was presented in November 1859 and printed in the Abhandlungen, Band 8 (1860). The letter therefore dates the surrounding calculations to roughly late 1859 or early 1860. They are the final working-out of what is now called Riemann's method of integrating the linear hyperbolic equation
 w_{rs} - m(w_r + w_s) = 0,
which arises in that paper.

The rest of the page holds very faint pencil calculations, apparently from an earlier use of the sheet. Several lines are heavily struck through. In the image one can make out the following, but no line is legible enough to reconstruct with certainty:
- fractions of partial derivatives;
- a word like 'geschrieben' with an underlined symbol below it;
- a short column of terms with ∂/∂σ-type derivatives on the left;
- in the lower middle, two-line integral expressions resembling ∫(…)(…)dσ and ∫(…)dσ'. These are consistent with the Fourier-integral and Wronskian formulas of the next page, which uses ψ1, ψ2, f, φ, χ(μ), ψ(μ) and the denominator fφ' − φf';
- further down, quotients of the form (A − B)/(C − D), again resembling (f(σ')φ'(σ) − φ(σ')f'(σ))/(f(σ)φ'(σ) − φ(σ)f'(σ)).

By context (my inference, not read from the page), the pencil work belongs to one of two strands:
- the Fourier-integral construction of the solution of w_{σσ} − 2m w_σ − w_{uu} = 0 from Cauchy data on σ = const (next page);
- the Green/Riemann function computations of the previous page, which involve v, ω, the variable z = −(σ−σ')²/(4σσ') + (u−u')²/(4σσ'), and v = (σ'/σ)^λ y.

No derivation on this page can be restated step by step from the image without inventing content.
